%% Query pipeline as actually implemented. Supersedes week2-query-sequence.mmd,
%% which predates the OpenAI embedding switch and the reranker rewrite.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant U as MCP Client (Claude Desktop / Cursor)
    participant M as server/main.py (FastAPI + MCP)
    participant S as search_filings.py
    participant QR as query_rewriter.py
    participant HR as hybrid_retriever.py
    participant BM as BM25 (in-memory, loaded from S3)
    participant OA as OpenAI (embeddings + gpt-4o-mini fallback)
    participant PC as Pinecone (finrag-filings, 1536-dim)
    participant RR as reranker.py
    participant AG as answer_generator.py
    participant NV as numerical_verifier.py
    participant BR as Bedrock (Haiku 4.5 / Sonnet 4.5)

    U->>M: call search_sec_filings(query)
    M->>S: build_search_filings_answer(query, ...)

    S->>QR: rewrite_query(query)
    QR->>BR: Converse -- expand tickers, extract time constraints
    alt Bedrock throttled or model not enabled
        QR->>OA: gpt-4o-mini fallback
    end
    QR-->>S: expanded query string

    par Hybrid retrieval (two threads)
        S->>HR: hybrid_search(rewritten, ...)
        HR->>BM: get_scores(tokenised query) -- top 10
        BM-->>HR: keyword hits
    and
        HR->>OA: embed(rewritten) -- text-embedding-3-small
        OA-->>HR: 1536-dim vector
        HR->>PC: query(vector, top_k=10, include_metadata=True)
        PC-->>HR: semantic hits
    end

    HR->>HR: merge INTERLEAVED by rank, dedup by chunk_id
    Note over HR: interleaving is load-bearing -- concatenating BM25<br/>then dense meant rerank's top-k slice was always<br/>100% BM25 and every dense hit was discarded
    HR-->>S: up to 20 candidates

    S->>RR: rerank(ORIGINAL query, candidates, top_k=5)
    alt CrossEncoder available (Lambda)
        RR->>RR: ms-marco-MiniLM-L-6-v2 scores each (query, chunk) pair
    else macOS + Python 3.13
        RR->>RR: lexical overlap scorer
        Note over RR: torch deadlocks on a mutex during the first<br/>forward pass locally; blind chunks[:k] is NOT a<br/>valid fallback since BM25 and cosine scores<br/>are not comparable across sources
    end
    RR-->>S: top 5 by relevance

    S->>AG: generate_answer(query, top_chunks)
    AG->>BR: Converse (Sonnet) -- cite every claim
    alt Bedrock throttled
        AG->>OA: gpt-4o-mini, retry w/ backoff on 429
    end
    AG-->>S: answer with inline [TICKER form period p.N] citations

    S->>NV: verify_answer(answer, source_texts)
    NV->>NV: regex-extract every number
    NV->>NV: boundary-aware grounding check per number
    Note over NV: "$1,234" is a substring of "$1,234.56" -- a naive<br/>`in` test passes fabricated figures. Replacement<br/>works by match span so an ungrounded number<br/>cannot corrupt a grounded one.
    NV-->>S: verified answer (ungrounded figures qualified)

    S-->>M: {answer, citations[{ticker,form,period,page,text}], cost_usd, latency_ms}
    M-->>U: cited answer rendered in chat

    Note over S: citations carry `text` -- the eval harness reads it<br/>as ragas `contexts`; omitting it scores every<br/>context metric as 0 against empty strings
